{"data":{"actor_id":"01KSK3QAE64QAADZ4Z86DY4771","created_at":"2026-10-04T05:12:33.637Z","event_type":"comment.status_changed","id":"103","payload":{"from":"open","reason":"FIXED in 32e5b664 — correct in full, and this was the finding that would have silently defeated the only push-path feature this PR adds.\n\nagent_setup.go hardcoded \"entire brain\". That is right only when a host entire CLI is on PATH; for a standalone install — no ENTIRE_CLI_VERSION, which setupCommandPrefix's own doc comment calls the common fallback — the invocation is `entire-brain`. The hook written into .claude/settings.json would have been a command that does not exist, failing on every edit without ever saying so: the same installed-and-inert failure this PR exists to fix, reintroduced by the fix.\n\nNow setupCommandPrefix(os.LookupEnv), matching agent_surface.go:1190, env.go:173, path.go:166.\n\nGuard: TestPreEditHookUsesTheGivenInvocation writes settings for both \"entire-brain\" and \"entire brain\" and asserts the file carries the invocation it was given.","to":"resolved"},"review_id":"01M420K6PSZTCRPEN85G1XVCPD","target_id":"01M420K6PZ7324PDZ1GEJVDNCE","target_type":"review_comment","trail_id":"01M3ZYBZG8PHYV8XPY98XXFB43"},"event":"comment.status_changed"}
{"data":{"actor_id":"01KSK3QAE64QAADZ4Z86DY4771","created_at":"2026-10-04T05:12:34.872Z","event_type":"comment.status_changed","id":"104","payload":{"from":"open","reason":"FIXED in 32e5b664 — the defect is real and reproduced. The prescribed remedy was rejected because adopting it breaks the feature outright, which is worth stating in full.\n\nREPRODUCED: with `.claude` a symlink to another directory, MergePreEditHook wrote 255 bytes outside the repository.\n\nFIXED: the read, the MkdirAll and the write now all go through an os.Root. The read is included deliberately — reading through an escaping symlink would merge a settings file from outside the repository and write the result back, so containment has to cover both ends.\n\nREMEDY REJECTED, with evidence: the suggestion was \"os.OpenRoot() + resolveContainedName like other file writes in this package\". The containment is right and is applied. resolveContainedName is not: it enforces an agent-instruction-file allowlist (AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, the guide) and refuses everything else with \"not an agent-instruction file\". .claude/settings.json is not one. Three pre-existing merge tests went red on exactly that error when I tried it — which is how this was caught rather than shipped. os.Root's own methods give the openat component resolution with no allowlist.\n\nMEASURED ATTRIBUTION, recorded in the test rather than assumed: all three contained calls reverted turns both escape tests red; keeping ANY ONE still refuses. So this is defence in depth, not three independent guards, and a sweep mutating one call at a time will report all three as unheld. The decisive check is reverting all three.","to":"resolved"},"review_id":"01M3ZYEYYJDWMKMMMXH6Z93YMF","target_id":"01M3ZYEYYSNFAQRBH3NM7VXKT3","target_type":"review_comment","trail_id":"01M3ZYBZG8PHYV8XPY98XXFB43"},"event":"comment.status_changed"}
{"data":{"actor_id":"01KSK3QAE64QAADZ4Z86DY4771","created_at":"2026-10-04T05:12:36.223Z","event_type":"comment.status_changed","id":"105","payload":{"from":"open","reason":"FIXED in 32e5b664 — correct, and the diagnosis was precise: line 134 opened a bare fence, six lines of prose sat inside it, and `sh` on line 143 read as a language specifier while actually being code-block content.\n\nTaking the second of the two suggested repairs, with one addition: the trapped paragraph was a near-duplicate of the activation note twelve lines above (README.md:121-128), so it is removed rather than relocated. The fence is now ```sh around the command alone.\n\nChecked after the edit: fence lines across the file total 40 (balanced), and no stranded bare language line remains outside a fence.","to":"resolved"},"review_id":"01M421MP2JX8EATEAXGAPKFVJR","target_id":"01M421MP2QH04VT7H2XQ9GXR4G","target_type":"review_comment","trail_id":"01M3ZYBZG8PHYV8XPY98XXFB43"},"event":"comment.status_changed"}
