{"data":{"actor_id":"01KSK3QAE64QAADZ4Z86DY4771","created_at":"2026-10-04T05:29:28.221Z","event_type":"comment.status_changed","id":"119","payload":{"from":"open","reason":"FIXED in 85973b89 — correct, and it is a regression I introduced: the fix traded a clear error for a hang.\n\nThe read is now gated on hookStdinWouldBlock, true only when the reader IS the process's stdin and that stdin is a character device — using stdinIsTerminal (seed.go:1811) as suggested. The check is on the READER, not just the process: a harness always redirects stdin and is read, a test with its own reader is read regardless of what the runner did with os.Stdin, and only a person at a terminal gets \"--file is required\".\n\nStated plainly: the hang is NOT reproducible in-process, because it needs a real character device on stdin and `go test` does not provide one. So the guards are the predicate (every non-stdin reader is read; os.Stdin tracks stdinIsTerminal) plus a call-site assertion, and the test says it is weaker than a behavioural one rather than implying otherwise. Ungating the call site turns the call-site guard red.","to":"resolved"},"review_id":"01M42N6V35JCDQDY9BFZPH94JT","target_id":"01M42N6V3PRADWNXEK1A4EB1R8","target_type":"review_comment","trail_id":"01M3ZYBZG8PHYV8XPY98XXFB43"},"event":"comment.status_changed"}
{"data":{"actor_id":"01KSK3QAE64QAADZ4Z86DY4771","created_at":"2026-10-04T05:29:29.362Z","event_type":"comment.status_changed","id":"120","payload":{"from":"open","reason":"FIXED in 85973b89 — correct arithmetic and correct remedy; taken as prescribed.\n\ntotal summed c over the LIMIT 6 rows, so with more than six distinct kinds it was a partial sum of the top groups. The sting is exactly as described: that note exists to give an agent an accurate picture after an empty result, and a too-low total risks the same false root cause it was written to prevent — the mistake that prompted writing it.\n\ntotal is now its own SELECT count(*) FROM symbols, with LIMIT 6 kept only for the displayed list.\n\nOne addition beyond the finding, same defect class: the kind COUNT is its own query too, so a truncated list reads \"(6 of 9 kinds)\" rather than presenting six of nine as the whole set. Six or fewer kinds reads exactly as before, pinned so the fix cannot pass by inflating every count.\n\nGuards: TestKindInventoryTotalCountsEveryKindNotJustTheTopSix (nine kinds, total must be 9, displayed must stay 6), TestKindInventoryIsExactBelowTheDisplayLimit, and two on the note text. Restoring the partial sum turns two of them red at once.","to":"resolved"},"review_id":"01M42N6V35JCDQDY9BFZPH94JT","target_id":"01M42N6V3D38AG3ZH7MQB30N39","target_type":"review_comment","trail_id":"01M3ZYBZG8PHYV8XPY98XXFB43"},"event":"comment.status_changed"}
