{"data":{"actor_id":"01KSK3QAE64QAADZ4Z86DY4771","created_at":"2026-10-04T06:03:03.950Z","event_type":"comment.status_changed","id":"148","payload":{"from":"open","reason":"FIXED in d36dd869 — correct, and it is an internal contradiction in code I wrote: the function's own doc comment promises the opposite of what it did.\n\nThe discarded second return value defaulted pre to nil whenever PreToolUse was present but not an array, and the append then wrote a brand-new one-element array over it. The user's configuration was destroyed silently. claudeHooksSection already makes exactly this check one level up for the hooks object, so the promise held for the container and not for the key being modified.\n\nNow routed through claudePreToolUseEntries, which refuses any non-array shape with the same message style as the hooks check. Absent or null is deliberately NOT an unrecognised shape: there is nothing to preserve, so the key is created as before.\n\nGuards: four unrecognised shapes (object, string, number, bool), each asserting the file is BYTE-IDENTICAL afterwards rather than merely that an error came back — the point is the data survives, not that a call failed. Plus five absent/empty/sibling cases asserting the hook still installs and a neighbouring PostToolUse survives the merge, so the refusal cannot pass by blocking every fresh install.","to":"resolved"},"review_id":"01M42PBSWTF7MF1V1VPW54F6P6","target_id":"01M42PBSX02H6DQBZ47D4SEKC4","target_type":"review_comment","trail_id":"01M3ZYBZG8PHYV8XPY98XXFB43"},"event":"comment.status_changed"}
