{"data":{"actor_id":"01KSK3QAE64QAADZ4Z86DY4771","created_at":"2026-10-04T20:34:03.448Z","event_type":"comment.status_changed","id":"229","payload":{"from":"open","reason":"FIXED in 05cbb55f — correct on both halves, and the merge framing is what makes it matter: repoRoot.WriteFile truncates in place, and this function MERGES, so a crash or full disk partway through destroys the user's pre-existing settings rather than just the hook entry being added.\n\nThe hard-link half is real too, and is the attack shape this package's own comments describe against .git/config.\n\nreplaceContainedFile cannot be reused, as suggested: it runs resolveContainedName, which admits only agent-instruction files and refuses .claude/settings.json outright — three pre-existing merge tests went red when that was tried earlier on this branch. So its sequence is repeated against the plain name: probe for write permission and shared inodes without truncating, preserve the original's permissions, stage beside the target, sync, rename.\n\nGuards: a merge over an existing file keeps the user's own keys and its 0600 mode and leaves no staging file; a hard-linked settings.json is refused and its other name is byte-identical afterwards. Reverting to the in-place write turns the hard-link test red.","to":"resolved"},"review_id":"01M43XZE6B6RA1DE14QR1EBCRZ","target_id":"01M43XZE6KGC3WSBGGN09NRR4B","target_type":"review_comment","trail_id":"01M3ZYBZG8PHYV8XPY98XXFB43"},"event":"comment.status_changed"}
{"data":{"actor_id":"01KSK3QAE64QAADZ4Z86DY4771","created_at":"2026-10-04T20:34:05.055Z","event_type":"comment.status_changed","id":"230","payload":{"from":"open","reason":"REFUTED — the nil dereference cannot occur; ModTime() is already inside the infoErr guard.\n\ninternal/cli/git_harden.go:\n\n  275  indexInfo, infoErr := indexFile.Stat()\n  276  contents, readErr := io.ReadAll(indexFile)\n  278  if readErr != nil { ... }\n  310  if infoErr == nil {\n  311      mtime := indexInfo.ModTime()\n\nLine 311 is reachable only when infoErr == nil, which is exactly when indexInfo is non-nil. The finding reads the readErr check at 278 as the only guard, but it is not the one protecting indexInfo — 310 is.\n\nThe behaviour when Stat() fails is deliberate and already stated in the comment above it: the mtime is simply not copied onto the scratch index. Without the original's mtime the copy is not a faithful stand-in, so the surrounding code falls back to the unmodified git command rather than risking a wrong answer.","to":"dismissed"},"review_id":"01M448V4WCRBZ0VN74B6QG1J83","target_id":"01M448V4WH9627FP0PS6YHM78Y","target_type":"review_comment","trail_id":"01M3ZYBZG8PHYV8XPY98XXFB43"},"event":"comment.status_changed"}
