{"data":{"actor_id":"01KSK3QAE64QAADZ4Z86DY4771","created_at":"2026-10-04T20:34:06.573Z","event_type":"comment.status_changed","id":"232","payload":{"from":"open","reason":"REFUTED — every call site already binds the 4-tuple, and the uncapped wrapper no longer exists to be called.\n\nProduction callers of detectRegressionAnomaliesCapped, all binding caps:\n\n  internal/cli/regression.go:1261   runRegressionDetect\n  internal/cli/regression.go:1506   runBrainReview\n  internal/cli/workspace.go:3668    scanWorkspaceRepoRegressions\n\nscanWorkspaceRepoRegressions returns caps.Truncated() (workspace.go:3679), both workspace result structs carry history_truncated, and reviewSummary / workspaceReviewSummary / regressionNoAnomaliesLine and the multi-repo headline all take the flag.\n\nThe specific risk named — silent truncation reported as complete — is what this change set removed, and it is guarded: TestNoUncappedRegressionDetectorRemains asserts the uncapped wrapper is absent and that both summaries receive a real flag rather than a literal false. grep confirms func detectRegressionAnomalies( appears nowhere outside that test's own assertion string.","to":"dismissed"},"review_id":"01M448V4WCRBZ0VN74B6QG1J83","target_id":"01M448V4WNMD0D88GCFB3AK5CA","target_type":"review_comment","trail_id":"01M3ZYBZG8PHYV8XPY98XXFB43"},"event":"comment.status_changed"}
