{"data":{"actor_id":"01KSK3QAE64QAADZ4Z86DY4771","created_at":"2026-10-04T22:25:35.488Z","event_type":"comment.status_changed","id":"279","payload":{"from":"open","reason":"CONFIRMED and FIXED in 253681bf (pushed as 1df3ba2d).\n\nReproduced. verifySemanticWorktreeStable (semantic.go:2925) -- which the code\ncredited with this guarantee -- re-checks worktree dirtiness and a worktree\nfingerprint. Both are measured against whatever HEAD is current, so\n`git commit --allow-empty` or a checkout while the provider runs leaves the\nworktree clean before and after and passes it. HEAD was never re-resolved.\n\nThe reason this bites only here: on every other path the provider stamps the\ncommit itself, so validateLiveSemanticHeader (semantic.go:746) compares the\nprovider's value against brain's pre-run `head` and a moved HEAD is already\nfatal. On the stamped path brain assigned its own `head` into header.Commit, so\nthat same comparison is a value against itself and cannot fail. The only path\nthat makes the \"verified unchanged\" claim was the only path with nothing\nbehind it.\n\nFix: verifySemanticHeadStable re-resolves HEAD and HEAD^{tree} after the\nprovider returns and refuses the index when either moved, called in the\n`res.stampedHeader != \"\"` block BEFORE the disclosure warning is emitted. The\nfirst of the finding's two remedies was taken (make the claim true) rather\nthan the second (delete the claim). Refusing rather than restamping with the\nnew HEAD is deliberate: the indexed content is a mixture of both commits, so\nneither describes it.\n\nRegression proof -- two compile-clean reverts, each fails a distinct assertion:\n\n1. Neuter the comparison (`_, _ = commitAfter, treeAfter; return nil`):\n   --- FAIL: TestStampedProvenanceRefusesAMovedHead\n       partial_clone_index_test.go:150: a HEAD that moved during indexing was\n       accepted, so the snapshot would be published stamped with a commit it\n       does not describe, claiming it was verified unchanged\n\n2. Remove the call site, leaving the function defined but unused (legal Go):\n   --- FAIL: TestStampedProvenanceIsVerifiedBeforeItIsDisclosed\n       partial_clone_index_test.go:188: the stamped path discloses that the\n       commit was verified unchanged without calling verifySemanticHeadStable\n       first, so nothing verifies it\n\nThe second test exists because the previous defect on this exact code path was\nan assignment placed in the wrong branch, not a missing function -- a unit test\non the helper alone would not have caught it. The test case that matters most\nis a new commit on an UNCHANGED tree: that is precisely the shape a dirtiness\ncheck cannot see. A failing git is covered too, and must not read as\n\"unchanged\".\n\nAlso corrected the comment above TestBrainStampsAHeaderTheProviderCouldNotStamp,\nwhich asserted in prose that verifySemanticWorktreeStable established this.","to":"resolved"},"review_id":"01M44D0RFCP65MEMSVV6Z8TJVZ","target_id":"01M44D0RFH560E384NKJVE2DCE","target_type":"review_comment","trail_id":"01M3ZYBZG8PHYV8XPY98XXFB43"},"event":"comment.status_changed"}
